+# Ops notes: credentials
+
+Values are not recorded here. Only names and locations.
+
+## Credentials in use
+
+| Name          | Used for                                          | Configured in |
+|---------------|---------------------------------------------------|---------------|
+| `CLOUD_TOKEN` | Bearer token for the hosting API (`http://127.0.0.1:8787`), all environments | `.env` (`ws/.env`) |
+
+Usage is documented in `ops/cloud.md` (`Authorization: Bearer $CLOUD_TOKEN`).
+
+## Non-secret configuration
+
+- `STAGING_DB`: path to the SQLite database. Set in `.env`; defaults to `data/staging.db` when unset (`app/db.py`). Not a credential.
+
+## Notes
+
+- `.env` holds the live token. Keep it out of version control and do not paste its value into tickets or logs.
+- The app code (`app/`) reads no credentials. Only `CLOUD_TOKEN` is needed for the hosting API.
